    "narrative": "With **Corbin Carroll** leading the way at an elite 85.94, our offensive strategy for today hinges on exploiting the high-xERA matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano. **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier weapon, as his combination of favorable platoon splits and batting order position makes him the clear anchor for our daily production. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17) also profile as high-end starts, benefiting significantly from the projected weakness in the opposing rotation. **Brice Turang** (68.98) continues to be a staple of our lineup; despite facing the formidable Walker Buehler, his leadoff spot and stolen base potential ensure he maintains a strong floor in our 5x5 framework.\n\nWe are navigating several delicate platoon decisions today, most notably with **Isaac Paredes** (59.40) and **Mickey Moniak** (60.31). While both are in the \"Strong\" start tier, they face regression risks due to platoon disadvantages against Carson Whisenhunt and Mitch Bratt, respectively. Conversely, **Max Muncy** (63.27) is a surprising riser; despite the low batting order slot, the park factors and the favorable matchup against Nick Martinez provide enough value to comfortably surpass the 60-point efficiency threshold. We are carefully monitoring **Jose Caballero** (46.23) and **Austin Riley** (46.88), both of whom are hovering in the marginal category; their starts are contingent on their presence in the final confirmed lineups, as any shift down the order could easily push them below our acceptable threshold.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Zach McKinstry** (43.02), who pushed for a UTIL spot but ultimately lost out due to a combination of poor BvP metrics against Tanner Bibee and a projected bottom-of-the-order start. We continue to manage the health of our depth, with **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remaining sidelined on the IL, limiting our ability to pinch-hit for the lower-scoring bench options. All projections currently assume standard lineup positioning; should any of our starters be rested, we are prepared to pivot to the remaining bench assets, though we must remain vigilant regarding the total game caps as we navigate the final stretch of the season.",
